ISO-10303-21;
/* Tsh260: OPEN_SHELL with TWO ADVANCED_FACEs forming a non-conformal T-junction. Face LONG hosts a full-length reference edge x=1,y:[0,2] (#10). Face SHORT hosts a free candidate edge x=1,y:[0.5,1.5] (#46) whose BOTH endpoints (1,0.5,0)/(1,1.5,0) lie STRICTLY in the interior of LONG's reference edge, sharing no vertex with it. A hanging-vertex / T-junction: BRepBuilderAPI_Sewing::Cutting splits the reference edge at the two projected interior nodes so the boundary becomes conformal. shape_null=False; 2 faces; sewing scaffold required (Cutting is not on the default STEP read path). */
